    "question": {
      ":question/id": "237de541-cfb4-554d-8752-8352e14542d0",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & 9 \\\\ -9 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 9 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}19 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of $a_{22}=-3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & 9 \\\\ -9 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 9 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}-3C_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}19 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}-C_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}19 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{1}:=C_{1}-3C_{2}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}-C_{2}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
